      "extract": "For many years, it was thought that Landau’s theory of symmetry breaking [1] could describe essentially all phases and phase transitions. It appeared that all con- tinuous phase transitions were associated with a broken symmetry. However, after the discovery of the fractional quantum Hall (FQH) eﬀect, it was realized that FQH states contain a new type of order - topological order - that is beyond the scope of Landau",
